>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Split`

``` hol4
simpLib.Split : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as a split rule for one simplifier call.

`Split th` in the theorem list of a simplifier call adds `th` to that
call's simpset as `add_split` does. A malformed rule is ignored with a
warning.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>> SIMP_TAC bool_ss [simpLib.Split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)]
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”) c;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_split`](#simpLib.add_split),
[`splitLib.SPLIT_TAC`](#splitLib.SPLIT_TAC),
[`simpLib.Cong`](#simpLib.Cong).
